Description: 'SQLECmd: process SQLite databases'
Category: SQLDatabases
Author: Andrew Rathbun
Version: 1.1
Id: f9198051-4899-465d-aa5a-8291525d82b1
BinaryUrl: https://download.ericzimmermanstools.com/SQLECmd.zip
ExportFormat: csv
Processors:
    -
        Executable: SQLECmd\SQLECmd.exe
        CommandLine: -d %sourceDirectory% --csv %destinationDirectory%
        ExportFormat: csv
    -
        Executable: SQLECmd\SQLECmd.exe
        CommandLine: -d %sourceDirectory% --json %destinationDirectory%
        ExportFormat: json

# Documentation
# https://github.com/EricZimmerman/SQLECmd
# https://leanpub.com/eztoolsmanuals
# Hunt mode is enabled by default in the latest version of SQLECmd and can be used to help identify SQLite databases within a dataset (check console window to see which SQLite databases don't have a Map)
# Hunt mode can also be used to parse SQLite databases which do not follow a strict naming convention, i.e. %timestamp%.SQLite
# An example of a SQLECmd Map that will require Hunt mode every time is Windows_TeraCopy_History.smap
